{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && cat > update.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Third turn: narrowed from the healthy plain paths to the recovery/resynchronization path and reproduced a failure locally. In draft/tmp/ws/omnipaxos/tests/probe4.rs a 3-node in-process cluster (NoSnapshot entries, batch_size 3) reaches the state 'one node V: accepted_idx 6, decided_idx 3, accepted round r1; healthy follower F: accepted_idx 6, decided_idx 6, compacted_idx 6; leader L0 crashed' and then V takes over via try_become_leader. F's handling of V's Prepare panics with 'attempt to subtract with overflow' at omnipaxos_storage/src/memory_storage.rs:103, inside V's attempt to collect log support. This local run is construction feedback, not a retained receipt, so the new investigation is recorded with the source account and an unresolved defect claim; a fixed-input experiment repeating exactly this prefix is the next action.\\\",\n  \\\"sources\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"storage_get_suffix_contract\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos/src/storage/mod.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 162,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 171,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"interface_statement\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"memstorage_suffix\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos_storage/src/memory_storage.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 100,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 110,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"sync_log\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos/src/storage/internal_storage.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 313,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 360,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"investigations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@stale_decided_sync\\\",\n      \\\"question\\\": \\\"When a node whose decided index lags its accepted index (crash-recovered before the latest decisions reached it, while its accepted index let every peer pass the trim bound) becomes leader, does the healthy follower's construction of the log update stay inside the follower's own compacted prefix, or can it ask for entries that no longer exist and fail?\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"follower_prepare\\\", \\\"logsync\\\", \\\"memstorage_suffix\\\", \\\"storage_get_suffix_contract\\\", \\\"sync_log\\\"],\n      \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"With snapshots disabled, \"'`create_log_sync` takes its non-snapshot branch and reads `get_suffix(common_prefix_idx)`; in the follower'\"'s Prepare handling the common prefix is the *preparing leader's decided index* whenever the follower's accepted round is newer than the preparing leader's accepted round. That index can be below the follower's own compacted index, which the trim bound does not prevent (the trim bound constrains accepted indexes, not decided indexes).\\\",\n      \\\"discriminator\\\": \\\"Repeat the exact prefix in a fixed harness: 3 nodes, NoSnapshot entries, batch_size 3, six entries accepted by all, one node held below decided 3 while the others decide 6, leader trims to 6 and the node misses the forwarded compaction, leader crashes, the healthy follower becomes the accepted leader while the stale node promises without accepting, then the stale node calls try_become_leader. Observe whether the healthy follower's Prepare handling completes or aborts.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@logsync_non_snapshot_branch\\\",\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"fact\\\",\n      \\\"statement\\\": \\\"\"'`SequencePaxos::create_log_sync(common_prefix_idx, other_logs_decided_idx)` takes the snapshot branch only when `T::Snapshot::use_snapshots()` is true AND `decided_idx > common_prefix_idx`; otherwise it builds the update as `suffix = get_suffix(common_prefix_idx)` with `sync_idx = common_prefix_idx`, and nothing on that path compares `common_prefix_idx` against this node'\"'s own \"'`get_compacted_idx()`. With a non-snapshot Entry type the branch is therefore always taken, and the follower'\"'s Prepare handling passes the preparing leader's \"'`decided_idx` as `common_prefix_idx` in the branch where the follower'\"'s promise reports a newer accepted round.\\\",\n      \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"Captured snapshot; reached from \"'`handle_prepare` (follower is at least as up-to-date as the preparing leader) with `T::Snapshot::use_snapshots() == false`, or with `decided_idx <= common_prefix_idx` for a snapshot-capable entry type.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\"follower_prepare\", \"logsync\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@memstorage_suffix_underflow\",\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"statement\": \"`MemoryStorage::get_suffix(from)` evaluates `self.log.get((from - self.trimmed_idx)..)` with an unchecked `usize` subtraction against the number of log entries removed by trimming. For `from < trimmed_idx` this panics with '\"'attempt to subtract with overflow' when overflow checks are enabled (dev profile, as used by the harness), and when they are disabled the wrapped index makes \"'`.get(..)` yield `None` so the function returns an empty `Vec` instead of the entry suffix. The Storage trait it implements instead specifies returning an empty `Vector` when entries do not exist for the complete interval and never specifies a panic.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"Captured snapshot; `get_suffix` (and `get_entries`, which subtracts and slices with the same assumption) called with an index below the storage'\"'s \"'`trimmed_idx`, reachable from the core through `InternalStorage::get_suffix` -> `create_log_sync`.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\"memstorage_suffix\", \"storage_get_suffix_contract\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"interpretations\": [\n    {\n      \"investigation_id\": \"@stale_decided_sync\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\"follower_prepare\", \"logsync\", \"memstorage_suffix\", \"storage_get_suffix_contract\", \"sync_log\"],\n      \"conclusion\": \"conditional\",\n      \"defect_claim\": \"unresolved\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source reading identifies a concrete gap: the follower-side log-update construction can request a suffix at an index below the requestor'\"'s own compacted index, and the in-memory storage implementation turns that request into an arithmetic panic (dev profile) rather than the empty suffix its trait requires. A non-retained local run (draft/tmp/ws/omnipaxos/tests/probe4.rs) reproduces exactly that: with v_stale = (accepted 6, decided 3, round r1), f_healthy = (accepted 6, decided 6, compacted 6) and the old leader crashed, f becomes the accepted leader; when v calls try_become_leader, f's Prepare handling panics with 'attempt to subtract with overflow' at omnipaxos_storage/src/memory_storage.rs:103 while computing its log update, and v's preconditions (decided 3 < f's compacted 6, accepted 6 at the trim bound) are unchanged by that panic. Because that execution is local construction feedback and not a retained receipt, this account claims only a conditional expectation, not an asserted defect.\\\",\n      \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n        \\\"The panic is raised by \"'`MemoryStorage` (a dependency crate in the same captured snapshot) while the core'\"'s call is legal per the \"'`Storage::get_suffix` contract, so responsibility is split between the core'\"'s choice of prefix and the storage implementation's unchecked subtraction; a fix in either location would remove the observed failure.\\\",\n        \\\"Upstream's trim bound (\"'`get_min_all_accepted_idx`) is what keeps other sync paths away from the compaction boundary, so this path needs the phase where the follower'\"'s accepted round is newer than the preparing leader's while the preparing leader's decided index is older than the trim point; a scenario without a crash-recovered node holding a stale decided index does not reach it.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"limitations\\\": [\n        \\\"The local reproduction is not a retained receipt; the next action repeats the same prefix as a fixed-input experiment in the omnipaxos package and cites its CheckRun.\\\",\n        \\\"The release-profile consequence (empty suffix instead of a panic, leaving \"'`sync_log` to set accepted_idx 3 with decided_idx 6) is a source-level inference in this update and was not measured.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\nJSON\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '\"'/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -5\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
